# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data is not redistributed.
# The CWRU 12 kHz drive-end and Paderborn KAt recordings are third-party public
# datasets and stay under their original terms. Rebuild them locally instead:
#     python tools/prepare_cwru.py        # downloads the 40 official CWRU files
# and see README.md for the Paderborn layout. Together they are ~15 GB, which
# no code repository should carry.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/

# Cached copies of the official downloads and the windowed .npz caches
# (keyed on a content fingerprint of the source files, so they invalidate
# whenever the data changes).
.cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build products of tools/make_supplementary.py. The package is assembled by
# copying files out of this repository, so committing it would duplicate the
# whole tree. supplementary.zip is what goes to the journal, not to git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
supplementary/
supplementary.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal working notes. 接手文档.md is a handover document in Chinese
# containing candid assessments of the method and the benchmarks, journal
# strategy and page-charge trade-offs. It is not written for readers of the
# paper; the material a reviewer needs (in particular the CWRU 99.mat defect)
# is in README.md and in the supplementary package's README.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
接手文档.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LaTeX intermediates. The sources, the bibliography, the figures and the
# compiled PDFs are tracked on purpose; everything regenerated by a compile
# is not. Keep paper/*.bbl if the manuscript is ever uploaded to arXiv.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
paper/*.aux
paper/*.blg
paper/*.log
paper/*.out
paper/*.spl
texput.log
*.synctex.gz

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
